   "id": "zevachim.89b.19",
   "daf": "89b",
   "sentenceId": 18,
   "he": "אָשָׁם קוֹדֵם לְתוֹדָה כּוּ׳. אַדְּרַבָּה – הַתּוֹדָה וְאֵיל נָזִיר קָדְמִי, שֶׁכֵּן טְעוּנִין לֶחֶם! אֲפִילּוּ הָכִי, קׇדְשֵׁי קָדָשִׁים עֲדִיפִי.",
   "en": "The mishna further teaches: «A guilt offering precedes a thanks offering» and the nazirite’s ram due to the fact that it is an offering of the most sacred order. The Gemara challenges: «On the contrary, the thanks offering and» the «nazirite’s ram» should «precede» the guilt offering, «as they require loaves» to be brought with them. The Gemara explains: «Even so,» the fact that the guilt offering is an «offering of the most sacred order» is of «greater» importance."
  }
